Author: Tomáš Bordák [xborda01]
Date: 18.11.2024

Description:

    PCAP to NetFlow v5 exporter written in C

    Program goes through every packet in pcap file, processes the packet headers and then manages
    to create a new flow or if packet is matching existing flow, it updates the existing flow with packet
    data. Processes ONLY TCP packets, ignores rest. Flows can expire only if active or inactive timeout is greater or equal to active_timout or inactive_timeout (default 60 seconds).
    Also if any flow doesnt expire when program is reading pcap file, after all packets, rest of flows get automatically exported.
    
    Program uses UDP to send (export) flows to collector. Sends UDP datagram with NetFlow v5 header and 30 NetFlow v5 flow records.
    30 is maximum per datagram. Only when the program is exporting the rest of flows, datagram can include <= 30 per datagram (if there is
    40 flows left -> first datagram with 30 flows and second with 10 flows, maximazing the datagram potential).
    

How to use:

    make

    ./p2nprobe <host>:<port> <pcap_file_path> [-a <active_timeout> -i <inactive_timeout> -h]

            <host>:<port> - host has to be either IPv4 address or hostname, that will get resolved to IPv4 address
                          - port has to be a number in range of 0 to 65535
                          - IS MANDATORY
                          - NO SUPPORT FOR IPv6 HOST

            <pcap_file_path> - path to file (enter just a file name, when the file is in the same directory)
                             - IS MANDATORY
            
            -a <active_timeout> - number of seconds to set the active timeout of the flow export
                                - DEFAULT 60
            
            -i <inactive_timeout> - number of seconds to set the inactive timeout of the flow export
                                  - DEFAULT 60

            -h - prints usage with detail description of options


Example use:

    ./p2nprobe localhost:2055 test_pcap_files/druhy_pcap.pcap 

    
